+  "comment": "Capability derived from PUBLISHED BENCHMARK SCORES. Replaces v1, where every benchmark field was a placeholder ('Frontier tier', 'Moonshot official') and the self_reported discount fired only on Chinese vendors - capping DeepSeek/Kimi at 0.63 while GPT/Claude sat at 1.00. Policy: (1) two task-matched axes - agentic_cli (Terminal-Bench 2.x) and agentic_swe (SWE-bench Pro/Verified); (2) self_reported is judged by HARNESS OWNERSHIP and applied identically to every vendor; (3) capability = normalized score on the slot's axis, x0.9 when self_reported; (4) scores are NOT comparable across harnesses - `harness` is recorded so the report can say which. v2.1: self_reported is now PER-AXIS (self_reported_cli / self_reported_swe) because a model can have an independent score on one axis and a vendor score on another - GPT-5.6 Sol is independently benchmarked on Terminal-Bench but its SWE-bench Pro figure comes from the same vendor aggregate as everyone else's. Also adds published $/Mtok so the optimizer can reason about VALUE (quality per unit spend), not just quality. v3: full OpenCode Go catalogue as of 2026-08-14 (19 models incl. Grok 4.5, GLM-5.3, Qwen3.8 Max, MiMo-V2.5, Hy3, and GPT-5.6 Luna which is available ON GO). Prices are Go's own published per-Mtok rates. go_usage_allowance_usd is the monthly usage Go includes for that model ($15 or $60) \u2014 models at $15 give a quarter the value of $60 models, which is the real generalization of the Kimi-K3 '2x usage' note.",
